WEBVTT

00:00:00.597 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.775 --> 00:00:06.340
In this lesson, we work together from the moment the client sits down in the chair,

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:08.190
until the hair has been shampooed,

00:00:08.445 --> 00:00:11.550
and divided into seven neat sections, ready to cut.

00:00:12.137 --> 00:00:14.590
You heard the reason for each step in the theory lesson.

00:00:14.956 --> 00:00:16.030
Here, we do it.

00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:17.409
Step one:

00:00:17.661 --> 00:00:19.409
welcome the client and get ready.

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:23.729
Wash your hands before you touch the client, as in the hand hygiene lesson.

00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:24.604
Combs,

00:00:24.554 --> 00:00:29.329
scissors and clips must have been cleaned and disinfected after the previous client.

00:00:29.838 --> 00:00:32.894
Wrap a disposable neck strip around the client's neck,

00:00:32.844 --> 00:00:35.009
and only then fasten the cape over it.

00:00:35.344 --> 00:00:38.049
The cape should never touch the skin of the neck directly.

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:39.488
Step two:

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.208
the consultation, while the hair is still dry.

00:00:42.844 --> 00:00:45.808
Ask what the client likes and doesn't like about their hair now.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:47.648
Ask to see a reference photo.

00:00:48.075 --> 00:00:51.294
Ask whether they blow-dry every morning or let it dry naturally,

00:00:51.244 --> 00:00:52.928
and whether they often tie it up.

00:00:53.437 --> 00:00:55.408
Agree on the length with a reference point:

00:00:55.674 --> 00:00:58.710
hold a section of hair, place it at exactly that spot,

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.368
and say it back to the client:

00:01:00.537 --> 00:01:02.768
we are cutting to shoulder level, is that right?

00:01:03.064 --> 00:01:06.688
If the hair is curly or wavy, tell the client beforehand.

00:01:06.948 --> 00:01:10.928
Once it is dry, the hair will shrink up, so we leave it a little longer.

00:01:11.106 --> 00:01:12.928
Write what you agreed in the client record.

00:01:13.046 --> 00:01:16.368
Next time, whoever does the cut will know what the client likes.

00:01:16.947 --> 00:01:17.737
Step three:

00:01:18.063 --> 00:01:21.017
check the hair and the scalp, still while it is dry.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.697
Pull the hair back, and look at the face shape and the hairline.

00:01:24.962 --> 00:01:26.137
Make a few partings:

00:01:26.326 --> 00:01:29.257
look at the density, the texture, and the scalp.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:33.977
Comb the hair in a few directions, and look for whorls at the crown and the nape.

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:38.059
If the scalp has a wound, inflammation, or lice, stop,

00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:40.377
and speak to the client privately.

00:01:40.622 --> 00:01:43.577
The lesson on when not to treat a client explains why.

00:01:44.232 --> 00:01:45.095
Step four:

00:01:45.277 --> 00:01:46.055
the shampoo.

00:01:46.597 --> 00:01:47.975
Take the client to the basin.

00:01:48.238 --> 00:01:52.059
Put a towel around the shoulders, support the neck as it rests in the basin,

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:53.895
and ask whether anything is pressing.

00:01:54.305 --> 00:01:57.128
If the client has neck or back problems, ask first,

00:01:57.078 --> 00:01:59.575
and adjust the chair so they are comfortable.

00:01:59.913 --> 00:02:02.535
Turn on the water, and test it on your own wrist.

00:02:02.881 --> 00:02:05.655
Then let the water touch the hair, and ask again:

00:02:06.023 --> 00:02:07.175
is the temperature okay?

00:02:07.411 --> 00:02:09.975
Wet the hair evenly, from roots to ends.

00:02:10.593 --> 00:02:13.431
Take just enough shampoo, and spread it evenly.

00:02:13.906 --> 00:02:17.140
Massage the scalp with your fingertips, in small circles,

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.431
from the front hairline back to the nape.

00:02:19.846 --> 00:02:21.111
Never use your nails.

00:02:21.357 --> 00:02:22.311
Rinse thoroughly.

00:02:22.649 --> 00:02:26.465
One hand holds the shower head, the other shields along the hairline,

00:02:26.415 --> 00:02:29.031
so water doesn't run into the face or the ears.

00:02:29.375 --> 00:02:32.347
Then apply conditioner to the mid-lengths and ends,

00:02:32.297 --> 00:02:36.071
leave it on as the product instructs, and rinse again thoroughly.

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:37.667
Step five:

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:38.787
towel-dry.

00:02:39.194 --> 00:02:40.707
Bring the client back to the chair.

00:02:41.118 --> 00:02:45.347
Wrap the hair in a towel, and press gently from the roots down to the ends.

00:02:45.616 --> 00:02:47.427
No rubbing, no scrunching.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.987
The hair should just be damp, not dripping.

00:02:50.616 --> 00:02:51.516
Step six:

00:02:51.696 --> 00:02:52.396
detangle.

00:02:52.812 --> 00:02:54.236
Use a wide-tooth comb.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:58.076
One hand holds the hair above, and the comb starts at the ends.

00:02:58.413 --> 00:03:03.356
Once the ends are free, work gradually higher, and higher, up to the roots.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:07.356
Your hand holds the hair, so the client feels no pulling on the scalp.

00:03:07.988 --> 00:03:08.813
Step seven:

00:03:09.065 --> 00:03:09.773
the parting.

00:03:10.177 --> 00:03:14.573
Find the client's natural parting, or a center parting, depending on the cut.

00:03:15.086 --> 00:03:17.854
Place the tip of the tail comb at the front hairline,

00:03:17.804 --> 00:03:19.853
and draw it straight back to the crown.

00:03:20.282 --> 00:03:24.093
The parting must be straight and clean, showing a clear line of scalp.

00:03:24.762 --> 00:03:25.458
Step eight:

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:26.978
the seven sections.

00:03:27.292 --> 00:03:28.898
First, the top section.

00:03:29.311 --> 00:03:32.578
From each temple, draw a straight line back to the crown.

00:03:33.005 --> 00:03:35.218
Twist that hair up, and clip it flat.

00:03:35.693 --> 00:03:37.458
Next come the side sections.

00:03:37.807 --> 00:03:41.138
Draw a line from the top of the ear, up to the top section.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:44.018
The hair in front of that line is the side section.

00:03:44.355 --> 00:03:45.538
Twist and clip.

00:03:45.887 --> 00:03:47.778
Do exactly the same on the other side.

00:03:48.429 --> 00:03:49.317
Then the back.

00:03:49.731 --> 00:03:53.243
Draw a straight center parting from the crown down to the nape,

00:03:53.193 --> 00:03:55.717
dividing the back into left and right halves.

00:03:56.147 --> 00:04:00.186
Then draw a horizontal line from behind one ear to behind the other,

00:04:00.136 --> 00:04:01.477
at the occipital bone,

00:04:01.746 --> 00:04:03.877
the part that sticks out a little at the back of the head.

00:04:04.375 --> 00:04:07.557
Above the horizontal line are the two upper back sections.

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:09.717
Below it are the two nape sections.

00:04:09.987 --> 00:04:11.477
Twist and clip each one.

00:04:11.723 --> 00:04:13.637
That gives you all seven sections:

00:04:13.717 --> 00:04:17.717
one top, two sides, two upper back, and two nape.

00:04:18.364 --> 00:04:19.793
A few tips for sectioning.

00:04:20.196 --> 00:04:24.273
Draw partings with the tip of the tail comb, in one continuous line;

00:04:24.382 --> 00:04:25.793
don't scratch back and forth.

00:04:26.128 --> 00:04:28.943
Twist the hair with moderate tension before clipping,

00:04:28.893 --> 00:04:32.753
and clip it flat against the head, so the hair doesn't pull on the scalp,

00:04:32.913 --> 00:04:35.153
and doesn't sit on the area you are about to cut.

00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:37.966
If a few strands stray into the next section,

00:04:37.916 --> 00:04:40.113
pick them back with the tail of the comb.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.713
Then check everything once, in the mirror and from behind:

00:04:43.982 --> 00:04:46.513
are the partings straight, are both sides even?

00:04:46.863 --> 00:04:49.553
Wherever something is off, comb it and redo it.

00:04:49.902 --> 00:04:52.593
A crooked parting means a crooked cut afterwards.

00:04:53.155 --> 00:04:54.034
Step nine:

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.114
keep the hair evenly damp.

00:04:56.717 --> 00:04:58.354
The hair dries as you work.

00:04:58.693 --> 00:05:03.296
With some parts dry and some wet, the strands stretch and shrink differently,

00:05:03.246 --> 00:05:04.834
and the cut won't be even.

00:05:05.249 --> 00:05:08.434
Mist lightly and evenly over the area you are about to cut.

00:05:08.782 --> 00:05:10.514
Just damp, never dripping.

00:05:10.863 --> 00:05:12.194
Now the hair is ready to cut.

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:14.270
After the client leaves:

00:05:14.454 --> 00:05:16.590
used towels go into the laundry basket.

00:05:16.918 --> 00:05:20.330
Combs, scissors and clips are cleaned and disinfected,

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.510
as in the lesson on cleaning tools.

00:05:22.939 --> 00:05:24.350
The neck strip goes in the bin.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:27.710
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
